  <note>
    <content textType="body">
      <p>Testing is where the walkthrough becomes trustworthy. There are 45 tests split across the pyramid - sixteen fast unit tests for rules and mapping, six slice tests that run the chain, and twenty-three web plus integration tests. The key principle is behavior over implementation: we assert what happened - the status, the stored state, the number of bank calls - not how the code did it. The integration suite even uses a real JDK HttpServer to prove timeout behavior with real sockets. CI enforces line and branch coverage gates, so a regression cannot quietly merge.</p>
    </content>
  </note>
